# TeLex-KG case-study graph, version 1.2.0
#
# Part 1 (real): the two examples in Section 5 of the paper, built by hand from the
#   official texts in the Croatian Official Gazette (Narodne novine). Acts are
#   identified by their ELI. Only the acts and provisions below are included; later
#   amendments are not.
# Part 2 (SYNTHETIC): invented acts under https://w3id.org/telex-kg/id/synthetic/,
#   showing cases the real examples do not. They are not real legal acts.
#
# Conventions
# - eli:first_date_entry_in_force  first day in force
# - eli:date_no_longer_in_force    LAST INCLUDED day in force
# - eli:date_applicability         first day of applicability
# - tlx:dateNoLongerApplicable     LAST INCLUDED day of applicability
#   The exclusive upper bound of the half-open intervals in the paper is the day after
#   the stored last day, and the event that closes an interval falls on that day.
# - tlx:opens / tlx:closes act on legal force; tlx:opensApplicability /
#   tlx:closesApplicability act on applicability.
# - An absent end is explained per dimension by tlx:openEnd (legal force) and
#   tlx:openApplicabilityEnd (applicability). Readings refer to the included sources.
# - A start of applicability equal to the start of legal force means that the act sets
#   no separate date of application. An end of applicability is never copied from the
#   end of legal force; each is justified separately.
# - Titles of acts use dcterms:title, because the domain of eli:title is eli:Expression.
# - Text units with tlx:text give the complete text of the provision; others point to
#   the official source with tlx:textSource.
# - IRIs under https://w3id.org/telex-kg/ are identifiers; they do not resolve.

@base    <https://w3id.org/telex-kg/id/> .
@prefix tlx:     <https://w3id.org/telex-kg/ontology#> .
@prefix eli:     <http://data.europa.eu/eli/ontology#> .
@prefix rdfs:    <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#> .
@prefix dcterms: <http://purl.org/dc/terms/> .
@prefix xsd:     <http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#> .
@prefix lang:    <http://publications.europa.eu/resource/authority/language/> .
@prefix country: <http://publications.europa.eu/resource/authority/country/> .

# ###########################################################################
# PART 1: REAL EXAMPLES
# ###########################################################################

