# ###########################################################################
# PART 2: SYNTHETIC EXAMPLES (NOT REAL LEGAL ACTS)
# All acts, provisions, dates and texts below are invented. Their IRIs are under
# https://w3id.org/telex-kg/id/synthetic/ and do not overlap with Part 1.
#
# A. Two consecutive versions of one article: legal force does not overlap, but the
#    first version still applies to proceedings started before the second entered
#    into force, so applicability overlaps under two rules. One article has ends
#    that have not been extracted.
# B. A termination condition with two requirements that affects legal force and
#    applicability. It is shown in its final, fulfilled state only; the earlier
#    unresolved state follows from the event dates at query time, so the graph
#    contains no contradictory states.
# ###########################################################################

# --- A. Transitional application ------------------------------------------

